From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:04:59 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero2: read the SPI NOR over
 two lines

The Zero2 schematic (v1.3) wires only SPI0_CLK, SPI0_CS0, SPI0_MOSI and
SPI0_MISO (PC0/PC3/PC2/PC4) to the 2MiB SPI NOR; WP# and HOLD# are not
connected to SPI0_WP/SPI0_HOLD (PC15/PC16, PC16 drives the USB1 VBUS
switch). MOSI and MISO can still act as IO0/IO1, so describe a 2-bit
receive bus. With the H616 dual mode support in spi-sun6i the SPI NOR
core then picks a 1-1-2 read from the flash's SFDP table instead of
the plain 0x03 READ it uses today.

The transmit side stays single-bit: page program over two lines is not
offered by the flash.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
@@ -156,5 +156,7 @@ &pio {
 &spi0 {
 	flash@0 {
 		vcc-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+		/* only CLK/CS0/MOSI/MISO reach the flash, so dual reads at most */
+		spi-rx-bus-width = <2>;
 	};
 };
